## Exp47 — Minimal Factorized Corridor Law — FROZEN BEFORE SCORE

Question: can robust components form a minimal 3-outcome law without Dwell?

Frozen formulas from original Exp41 TRAIN predictions:
p_exit_base(H)=1-P_no_exit_base(H).
q_adv_pos(H)=CIF_adv_position(H)/(CIF_adv_position(H)+CIF_rec_position(H)).
P_fact(no_exit)=1-p_exit_base.
P_fact(advance)=p_exit_base*q_adv_pos.
P_fact(recapture)=p_exit_base*(1-q_adv_pos).

Reuse exact Exp41 eligible horizons 15/30/60/120 and exact 8 Exp44/45 environments. Primary comparison FACTOR_POSITION vs BASE_SURV using multiclass Brier and LogLoss, state-horizon weighted, whole-BRT-day bootstrap. Require >=70% coverage and all 3 classes per environment. Formal PASS requires lower 95% CI >0 for both metrics in all 8 environments: 16/16.

MINIMAL_FACTORIZED_CORRIDOR_LAW=PASS only at 16/16. ROBUST_MINIMAL_CORRIDOR_EQUATION=PASS only if all environments scorable and 16/16.

